/// Assertions and test-only operations for `test "name" { ... }` items. Each one returns `Void` when it
/// holds, and otherwise ends the test with a failure that `chimi test` reports
/// with the assertion's location and both values in the debug format.
///
/// A failed assertion is a defect, not an expected failure, so it works inside
/// a fake's method and code under test cannot recover from it. Assertions are
/// ordinary functions, so a program may also use them to check an invariant.

import std/process as Process

/// Fails unless `actual == expected`, with the same structural equality the
/// program uses. The actual value comes first, so a pipeline reads in the
/// order the work happens: `parse("12") |> Test.assert_equal(12)`.
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of both values.
pub native fn assert_equal<T>(actual: T, expected: T) -> Void

/// Fails when `actual == expected`, and shows both values.
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of both values.
pub native fn assert_not_equal<T>(actual: T, expected: T) -> Void

/// Fails with `message` unless `condition` holds, as in
/// `Test.assert(count > 3, "count is above 3")`. The message says what was
/// being checked.
///
/// Cost: O(1).
pub native fn assert(condition: Bool, message: Text) -> Void

/// Fails the test with `message`, as in a fake method that must not be
/// called. It never returns.
///
/// Cost: O(1).
pub native fn fail(message: Text) -> Never

/// Runs `operation` and returns the message of the defect it raised, so a
/// test can check a precondition:
/// `Test.capture_defect(fn() { checkout(0) }) |> Test.assert_equal(message)`.
/// Tasks the operation started are cancelled and drained first.
///
/// When `operation` succeeds or fails with an expected failure, the test
/// fails, naming what happened instead. An assertion failure inside
/// `operation` is not captured: it ends the test as usual. Test-only: a
/// program whose `main` reaches it does not build (`T4401`).
///
/// Calls: `operation` once.
/// Cost: O(1) plus `operation`.
pub native fn capture_defect<T, F, R>(operation: fn() -> T errors F needs R) -> Text needs R

/// An append-only log of values a fake recorded, owned by the test run. It is
/// shareable, so a fake running in another task can record into it. It renders
/// as `<Recorder>` and has no equality.
pub native type Recorder<T>

/// A queue of replies a scripted fake hands out one at a time. It is shareable
/// and renders as `<Script>`.
pub native type Script<T>

/// A new, empty recorder. Test-only (`T4401`).
///
/// Cost: O(1).
pub native fn recorder<T>() -> Recorder<T>

/// Appends `value` to `recorder`. `T` must be shareable (`T4403`), because
/// `recorded` hands the same value out again. Test-only (`T4401`).
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of `value`.
pub native fn record<T>(recorder: Recorder<T>, value: T) -> Void

/// Every value recorded so far, oldest first. Records from several tasks
/// appear in the order they happened. Test-only (`T4401`).
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of the recorded values.
pub native fn recorded<T>(recorder: Recorder<T>) -> List<T>

/// A script that hands out `replies` in order. `T` must be shareable
/// (`T4403`). Test-only (`T4401`).
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of `replies`.
pub native fn script<T>(replies: List<T>) -> Script<T>

/// Removes and returns the script's next reply. Past the last one, the test
/// fails as an assertion: "script exhausted after N values". Test-only
/// (`T4401`).
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of the reply.
pub native fn next<T>(script: Script<T>) -> T

/// The receiving end of a fake process address from `mailbox`. It is not a
/// `Process.Inbox`: `Process.receive` does not take it, and it renders as
/// `<Mailbox>`. It is shareable, so any task may read it.
pub native type Mailbox<M>

/// A fake process address that no process owns, and the mailbox that holds
/// what is sent to it. `Process.send` to the address follows the mailbox rules:
/// it never parks, and it fails with `SendError.Full(message)` once `capacity`
/// messages are held. The address equals only itself and renders as
/// `<address test>`. Test-only (`T4401`), and native-only, as processes are.
///
/// Defects when: `capacity` is below 1.
/// Cost: O(1).
pub native fn mailbox<M>(capacity: Int) -> (Process.Address<M>, Mailbox<M>)

/// Every message delivered to `mailbox` since the last call, in delivery
/// order. It removes them, which frees capacity. Test-only (`T4401`).
///
/// Cost: O(n) in the size of the messages.
pub native fn received<M>(mailbox: Mailbox<M>) -> List<M>
